cards.text:
{red|**Think about what's beneath your typical conflict behavior.**

When you do what you do in conflict: • What are you actually feeling?}{red| (Not what you show, but what you feel) • What are you afraid will happen?}{red| • What do you need in that moment?}

Be honest—this is for your growth:

{red|**Now try to imagine your spouse's experience.**

When they do what they do in conflict: • What might they actually be feeling underneath?}{red| • What might they be afraid of?}{red| • What might they really need?}

Try to write from their perspective with compassion:

{red|This week, track your triggers:

1. What triggered you?}{red| 2. Body sensation?}{red| 3. Emotion?}{red| 4. Thought?}{red| 5. What did you do?}

**Just build awareness.** That's the foundation for change.

{red|For pursuers: What's the hardest part about pulling back?}

{red|For withdrawers: What's the hardest part about staying present?}

Write your honest reflection:

{red|What has your conflict pattern cost you?}{red| Your relationship?}{red| Your intimacy?}{red| Your peace?}

{red|What would be different if it changed?}

Write honestly about what's at stake:

{red|Based on your pattern, what strategies might work?}

{red|• What phrase to name the pattern?}{red| • What to say to pause?}{red| • How to communicate what's underneath?}

Write your plan:

{red|Envision healthier conflict:

• How would conversations start?}{red| • What would you do instead of your old pattern?}{red| • How would conflicts end?}

Describe your vision:

{red|Pick one specific new behavior to practice:

• Asking 'Is now a good time?}{red|' before raising issues • Staying in the room instead of leaving • Saying 'I need a break but I'll be back' • Expressing the feeling underneath instead of the criticism

What's your one new step?}

{red|How has your role in the pattern affected your spouse?}

{red|If you're the pursuer: Has your criticism made them feel inadequate?}

{red|If you're the withdrawer: Has your shutdown made them feel unloved?}

Write what you think your pattern has cost them:

{red|**Imagine your marriage twenty years from now.**

If you keep old patterns, where will you be?}

{red|If you establish new ones, what could your marriage look like?}

{red|What do you want your children to remember about how you handled conflict?}
